<title>INDIA: American Express cuts Indian prime lending rate.</title>
<headline>American Express cuts Indian prime lending rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Express Bank is reducing its Indian prime lending rate to 17.25 percent from 18.50 percent per annum effective November 1, an official said.</p>
<p>The maximum spread above prime lending rate would be 4.0 percent, she said.</p>
<p>The bank's decision is in line with that of most other banks which have reduced their lending rates after the October 19 monetary policy statement of the Reserve Bank of India, which boosted liquidity and prompted interest rate cuts.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
